{#
  The whitepaper cover header, used when front matter says `header: cover`.
  Everything here is driven by front matter keys that already exist in
  SHORTCODES.md. No key was invented for it.

  TOP RIGHT IS THE DATE, NOT AN EDITION. The Reference calls that slot
  "edition/date" and the frontmatter vocabulary has no `edition` key. Rather
  than invent one, it renders `updated`, through the same two filters the
  standard byline uses, so the visible string and the machine date cannot
  disagree by a day. If an explicit edition string is ever wanted, that is a new
  frontmatter key and a SHORTCODES.md row, not a silent addition here.

  THE META GRID RENDERS ONLY THE FIELDS A DOCUMENT HAS. Three columns, and each
  cell is conditional, so a piece without a reading time gets two filled cells
  rather than a labelled blank. The Reference specifies three columns and does
  not say which fields go in them; these are the frontmatter keys that describe
  a document rather than its content, in the order a reader wants them.
#}
<header class="cs-cover">
  <div class="cs-cover__top">
    <span class="cs-cover__kind">{{ kind }}</span>
    <span class="cs-cover__edition">
      <time datetime="{{ updated | isoDate }}">{{ updated | calendarDate }}</time>
    </span>
  </div>

  {#- h1 and deck are one group, so the panel's 40px gap separates the three
      sections and the deck's own 24px separates it from the title. -#}
  <div class="cs-cover__title">
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    {% if deck %}<p class="cs-cover__deck">{{ deck }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>

  {#- author resolves against _data/authors.js exactly as the standard byline
      does, and falls back to the raw key, which is obviously wrong and
      greppable rather than silently blank. -#}
  {%- set byline = authors[author] -%}
  <dl class="cs-cover__meta">
    {% if author %}
    <div class="cs-cover__field">
      <dt>Author</dt>
      <dd>{{ byline.name if byline else author }}</dd>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if readingtime %}
    <div class="cs-cover__field">
      <dt>Reading time</dt>
      <dd>{{ readingtime }} min</dd>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if reviewed %}
    <div class="cs-cover__field">
      <dt>Reviewed</dt>
      <dd>{{ reviewed }}</dd>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </dl>
</header>
